# Line endings are normalised in the repository, decided here rather than by
# whatever core.autocrlf each machine happens to have.
#
# Copied from raven-api, which learned this on 2026-09-02: a station branch
# arrived having rewritten three files to CRLF. Its actual change was 813 lines;
# the diff read as 4,513 insertions and 3,705 deletions, and it would have
# conflicted with every other branch touching those files. Nothing in a diffstat
# says "this is only line endings", so the rewrite is invisible until someone
# thinks to run `git diff --ignore-all-space`.
#
# raven-app had no such file and hit the identical problem on 2026-09-15: a
# 252-line change committed as 1,892 insertions and 1,671 deletions across three
# files. Tools that write a file back with the platform's endings are normal on
# Windows, so this is the only place it can be stopped for good.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows launchers must keep CRLF — cmd.exe and wscript mis-parse LF-only files.
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.vbs  text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
